@gateway = http://localhost:7206
@gateway2 = http://localhost:7216

# The WebSocket itself is ws://localhost:7206/ws?user=<id>&role=rider|driver.
# HTTP clients cannot hold it open; use `pnpm watch:ws` (see docs/HOW-TO-RUN.md) to see the messages.

### Connections, subscribed channels and forwarded messages on instance 1
GET {{gateway}}/admin/stats

?? status == 200
?? js typeof response.parsedBody.riders === "number"
?? js typeof response.parsedBody.channels === "number"
?? js typeof response.parsedBody.tripEvents.seen === "number"

### The same on instance 2
GET {{gateway2}}/admin/stats

?? status == 200
?? js typeof response.parsedBody.messagesOut === "number"

### A plain HTTP request to the WebSocket path is not an upgrade: 404
GET {{gateway}}/ws

?? status == 404
